              '“Beneficiary”: Indifferently the Professional Beneficiary and/or the Non-Professional Beneficiary.',
              '“Client”: Any visitor, guest or member of the clientele of the Professional Beneficiary.',
            ],
          },
        ],
      },
      {
        num: 'II',
        title: 'Purpose and Validity of the Offer',
        blocks: [
          { type: 'p', html: 'These General Terms and Conditions of Sale govern the relationship between the Service Provider, the Beneficiary and the Client and specify the conditions of performance of the services offered by the Service Provider. The Beneficiary accepts these conditions without reservation and guarantees their acceptance by the Client upon signing the quote and/or commercial proposal. These General Terms and Conditions of Sale are expressly published on www.carsitting.fr, and the Service Provider undertakes to provide these General Terms and Conditions of Sale to any Beneficiary and Client upon request.' },
          { type: 'p', html: 'The validity period of the offer is 1 month from the date of delivery of the offer, namely a quote and/or a commercial proposal.' },
          { type: 'p', html: 'Any derogation from the GTCS requires a written agreement.' },
        ],
      },
      {
        num: 'III',
        title: 'Pricing, Payment Terms, Invoicing & Late Payment Penalties',
        blocks: [
          { type: 'h3', text: '3.1. Regular service:' },
          { type: 'p', html: 'Pricing is subject to a written agreement between the Service Provider and the Beneficiary and applies for the first twelve months of the commercial relationship. The Parties agree that pricing shall be automatically revised annually on the contract anniversary date, such that the pricing in year n+1 shall increase by at least 2% compared to year n.' },
          { type: 'p', html: 'The Beneficiary undertakes to pay for the service by cheque payable to “CARSITTING”, or by bank transfer, at the end of each month.' },
          { type: 'p', html: 'Payment shall be made upon presentation of an invoice issued in the name of the Beneficiary. The Service Provider shall issue an invoice at the beginning of the month in the name of the Beneficiary and send it by email. Upon request, the Beneficiary may receive a paper copy of the invoice. The payment term is 30 days from invoice issuance.' },
          { type: 'p', html: 'In the event of non-compliance with any of the aforementioned payment conditions or a dispute relating to payment for services from previous month(s), the Service Provider reserves the right to suspend or cancel the provision of the service and/or suspend performance of its obligations.' },
          { type: 'h3', text: '3.2. One-off service:' },
          { type: 'p', html: 'In the case of a one-off event-type service, pricing is generally a flat fee based on a predefined duration. Any overtime shall be billed additionally in ½-hour increments pro rata to the rate billed for the initially planned service. Payment shall be made by cheque, cash or bank transfer upon receipt of the invoice. The maximum payment term is 30 days from the date of performance of the service. In the case of a one-off service, a 30% deposit must be paid upon signing the quote and/or commercial proposal. Failing payment of the deposit, CARSITTING reserves the right to cancel the service.' },
          { type: 'h3', text: '3.3. Late payment penalties:' },
          { type: 'p', html: 'In the event of late payment of a due invoice, late payment penalties may apply. The applicable interest rate shall be equal to the key interest rate in force at the European Central Bank (ECB) on 1 January or 1 July of the relevant calendar year, plus 10 percentage points.' },
          { type: 'p', html: 'In addition to late payment penalties, a fixed recovery fee of €40 (unless the debtor is in collective insolvency proceedings) shall be invoiced.' },
          { type: 'p', html: 'Additional compensation may be claimed from the debtor where recovery costs exceed €40, upon presentation of supporting documents.' },
        ],
      },
      {
        num: 'IV',
        title: 'Liability and Warranties of the Service Provider',
        blocks: [
          { type: 'p', html: 'In the event of a vehicle accident while in the care of the Service Provider’s valet, the Service Provider shall file the accident report with its insurance company and use its assistance service.' },
          { type: 'p', html: 'In the event of damage caused by the Service Provider’s valet in the performance of their duties, the Service Provider’s liability may in no case be incurred if:' },
          {
            type: 'ul',
            items: [
              'The vehicle entrusted by the Client was not, at the time of the damage, compliant with road traffic regulations (e.g. registration certificate, roadworthiness test, etc.);',
              'The Client failed to disclose to the valet, when handing over the keys, information useful for the proper operation of the vehicle or one or more defects of the vehicle, and such failure to inform was the partial or total, direct or indirect cause of the damage.',
            ],
          },
          { type: 'p', html: 'The Service Provider disclaims all liability with respect to vehicles left in the care of the Service Provider’s valet after the closing of the establishment or the end of the one-off event.' },
          { type: 'p', html: 'The Service Provider’s liability may in no case be incurred in the event of:' },
          {
            type: 'ul',
            items: [
              'Loss or theft of personal belongings and valuables inside the vehicle.',
              'Direct or indirect damage to such personal belongings and valuables.',
              'Carjacking or damage to the vehicle caused by third-party violence.',
            ],
          },
          { type: 'p', html: 'In the event of loss or theft of the vehicle keys between the time they were handed over to the valet and the time of their return, the Service Provider undertakes to notify the Beneficiary and the Client owning the lost or stolen keys and shall bear the cost of replacing said keys.' },
          { type: 'p', html: 'In any event, the Service Provider shall in no case be held liable for any failure to perform any of its obligations under these General Terms and Conditions of Sale, and/or for any direct or indirect loss resulting from a case of force majeure or a fortuitous event as defined by the French Civil Code.' },
        ],
      },
      {
        num: 'V',
        title: 'Obligations of the Service Provider – Right of Withdrawal',
        blocks: [
          { type: 'p', html: 'In carrying out its duties and services, the Service Provider undertakes to exercise all due care in accordance with best industry practices.' },
          { type: 'p', html: 'The Beneficiary determines the service to be performed; the Service Provider selects the necessary staff and the tasks to be carried out by each of its employees.' },
          { type: 'p', html: 'The Service Provider further undertakes towards the Non-Professional Beneficiary to provide all information relating to the services, pricing and terms of performance no later than upon delivery of a quote and/or commercial proposal and in any event prior to the conclusion of an agreement defining the conditions and terms of the provision of services by the Service Provider.' },
          { type: 'p', html: 'The Non-Professional Beneficiary, excluding the Professional Beneficiary, has the right to exercise their right of withdrawal within fourteen days from the written agreement with the Service Provider setting out the conditions and terms of the agreed service(s). However, if the service is to begin before the expiry of said withdrawal period and/or the Non-Professional Beneficiary wishes the Service Provider to perform one or more services before the expiry of the period, the Non-Professional Beneficiary must expressly waive the benefit of their right of withdrawal and inform the Service Provider by any written means.' },
        ],
      },
      {
        num: 'VI',
        title: 'Obligations of the Beneficiary and the Client',
        blocks: [
          { type: 'h3', text: 'Obligations of the Beneficiary:' },
          { type: 'p', html: 'The Beneficiary shall make available to the Service Provider all information or documents that may contribute to the proper performance of the service. To this end, the Beneficiary shall designate a dedicated point of contact to ensure communication throughout the duration of the service.' },
          { type: 'p', html: 'The Beneficiary guarantees to the Service Provider compliance by Clients with the obligations incumbent upon them under these General Terms and Conditions of Sale.' },
          { type: 'h3', text: 'Obligations of the Client:' },
          { type: 'p', html: 'Upon receiving the valet ticket from the Service Provider, the Client accepts these General Terms and Conditions of Sale and, consequently, all obligations incumbent upon them.' },
          { type: 'p', html: 'The Client must disclose to the Service Provider’s valet, when handing over the keys, any information useful for the proper operation of the vehicle and/or any known defect of said vehicle.' },
          { type: 'p', html: 'The Client undertakes to hand over to the Service Provider’s valet their vehicle emptied of all personal belongings and valuables.' },
          { type: 'p', html: 'Where the Access formula has been selected by the Beneficiary, the Client shall pay the sum of €10 (contractually predefined) upon return of their vehicle, which the Beneficiary guarantees.' },
        ],
      },
      {
        num: 'VII',
        title: 'Term of Commitment for a Regular Service',
        blocks: [
          { type: 'p', html: 'Unless otherwise agreed, any Regular Service shall take effect from the date of signature of the contract or acceptance by the Beneficiary of the Service Provider’s commercial offer and shall remain valid for an indefinite duration which may not, however, be less than twelve months.' },
        ],
      },
      {
        num: 'VIII',
        title: 'Renewal – Termination Terms',
        blocks: [
          { type: 'h3', text: '8.1. Regular service:' },
          { type: 'p', html: 'Either party may terminate the contract binding the Service Provider and the Beneficiary by notifying the other party of its decision not to renew said contract, by registered letter, observing a notice period of at least three months between the contract anniversary date and the date of first presentation of said registered letter.' },
          { type: 'h3', text: '8.2. One-off service:' },
          { type: 'p', html: `Any request by the Beneficiary to cancel a service must be sent at least 48 hours before the date of the service either by telephone (${phone1} / ${phone2}) or by email (${mail}).` },
          { type: 'p', html: 'The deposit amount will then be refunded in full. Otherwise, the deposit will be retained.' },
        ],
      },
      {
        num: 'IX',
        title: 'Insurance Policy',
        blocks: [
          { type: 'p', html: 'The Service Provider undertakes to take out an insurance policy with Covea Fleet, located at 160 Rue Henri Champion, 72100 – Le Mans, France.' },
          { type: 'p', html: 'This insurance policy covers the Service Provider up to €1,800,000 for property damage and up to €8,000,000 for bodily injury.' },
          { type: 'p', html: 'The Service Provider undertakes to provide, at the request of the Beneficiary or a Client, a copy of the insurance certificate upon simple request.' },
        ],
      },
      {
        num: 'X',
        title: 'Non-Solicitation of Staff',
        blocks: [
          { type: 'p', html: 'Each Party expressly refrains from soliciting for employment or hiring, directly or indirectly, any employee or collaborator of the other party, whether salaried or not, even if the initial solicitation is made by the collaborator. Each Party guarantees the application of this prohibition to the other companies of the Group to which it belongs. This prohibition applies throughout the duration of the commercial relationship and for twelve (12) months following its termination, for whatever reason.' },
          { type: 'p', html: 'In the event of a breach of this prohibition, the defaulting party shall be required to pay immediately to the other party, as a penalty clause, a lump-sum indemnity equal to twelve (12) months of the last gross monthly salary of the person solicited or hired, plus all recruitment costs for a replacement.' },
        ],
      },
      {
        num: 'XI',
        title: 'Commercial References',
        blocks: [
          { type: 'p', html: 'The Professional Beneficiary agrees that the Service Provider may include the services performed on its behalf among its commercial references.' },
        ],
      },
      {
        num: 'XII',
        title: 'Personal Data',
        blocks: [
          { type: 'p', html: `For the purposes of its business, the Service Provider is required to collect personal data of Clients and/or the Non-Professional Beneficiary and/or the staff of the Professional Beneficiary. In this respect, the Service Provider undertakes to comply with the provisions of the General Data Protection Regulation (GDPR) in the processing of personal data. The Service Provider guarantees that all data collected will be processed lawfully, fairly and transparently, and will only be used for the specific purposes for which it was collected. In addition, the Service Provider undertakes to implement appropriate technical and organisational measures to ensure an adequate level of security to protect personal data against unauthorised access, disclosure, alteration or destruction. Clients and/or the Non-Professional Beneficiary and/or members of the staff of the Professional Beneficiary have the right to access, rectify, erase or object to the processing of their personal data, in accordance with the GDPR, simply by contacting the Service Provider at the following email address: ${mail}. The Service Provider undertakes to inform them clearly and transparently about how their data is collected, used and stored, as well as their data protection rights. By accepting these terms, Beneficiaries acknowledge having read the Service Provider’s privacy policy, consent to the processing of their personal data in accordance with the GDPR, and guarantee acceptance by Clients of the processing of their personal data.` },
        ],
      },
      {
        num: 'XIII',
        title: 'Disputes – Mediation',
        blocks: [
          { type: 'p', html: 'In accordance with Article L. 612-1 of the French Consumer Code, the Client and/or the Non-Professional Beneficiary has the right to submit a request for amicable resolution by mediation regarding a written complaint addressed to the professional.' },
          { type: 'p', html: 'CARSITTING has designated, under registration number 52197/VM/2401, SAS Médiation Solution as its consumer mediation entity.' },
          { type: 'p', html: 'To refer a matter to the mediator, the Client and/or Non-Professional Beneficiary must submit their request:' },
          {
            type: 'ul',
            items: [
              'In writing to: Sas Médiation Solution - 222 chemin de la bergerie 01800 Saint Jean de Niost',
              `By email to: ${medMail}`,
              `Or by completing the online form entitled “Saisir le médiateur” on ${medUrl}`,
            ],
          },
          { type: 'p', html: 'Regardless of the method used, the request must include:' },
          {
            type: 'ul',
            items: [
              'The applicant’s postal, telephone and email contact details,',
              'The name, address and registration number with Sas Médiation Solution of the professional concerned,',
              'A brief statement of the facts,',
              'A copy of the prior complaint,',
              'All documents enabling the review of the request (purchase order, invoice, proof of payment, etc.)',
            ],
          },
          { type: 'p', html: 'In any event, any complaint is only admissible within 8 days after completion of the service concerned.' },
          { type: 'p', html: 'These General Terms and Conditions of Sale are governed solely by French law. Any dispute of any nature whatsoever relating to the performance of the service shall, failing amicable agreement, fall under the exclusive jurisdiction of the Paris Commercial Court (Tribunal de Commerce de Paris).' },
        ],
      },
    ],
  },
}[lang];
---
<Base title={copy.title} description={copy.description}>
  {/* Ouverture sobre : pas de photo, un titre et l'ornement de la charte. data-hero pour l'apparition en douceur. */}
  <section data-hero class="s-nuit px-6 pb-16 pt-36 text-center md:pb-24 md:pt-48">
    <p class="label hero-reveal mb-8">{copy.label}</p>
    <h1 class="display hero-reveal">{copy.h1}</h1>
    <p class="hero-reveal mt-6 font-serif text-xl italic text-ivoire-muted">{copy.effective}</p>
    <div class="hero-reveal"><Ornament /></div>
  </section>

  <section class="s-ivoire px-6 py-16 md:py-24">
    <div class="mx-auto grid max-w-6xl gap-12 lg:grid-cols-12 lg:gap-16">
      {/* Sommaire : visible à partir de 1024 px, il reste à l'écran pendant la lecture. */}
      <nav class="hidden lg:col-span-3 lg:block" aria-label={copy.toc}>
        <div class="sticky top-32">
          <p class="label mb-6">{copy.toc}</p>
          <ol class="space-y-3 border-l border-or/35 pl-6">
            {copy.sections.map((s, i) => (
              <li><a href={`#section-${i + 1}`} class="legal-toc"><span class="mr-3 font-serif italic text-or">{s.num}</span>{s.title}</a></li>
            ))}
          </ol>
        </div>
      </nav>

      <div class="lg:col-span-9 min-w-0">
        {copy.note && <p class="mb-10 border-l border-or/35 pl-6 text-sm italic text-ivoire-muted">{copy.note}</p>}

        <div class="space-y-16 md:space-y-20">
          {copy.sections.map((s, i) => (
            <article id={`section-${i + 1}`} class="scroll-mt-32">
              <div class="flex items-baseline gap-5">
                <span class="font-serif text-4xl font-light italic text-or">{s.num}</span>
                <h2 class="font-serif text-[28px] font-normal leading-tight text-nuit md:text-[34px]">{s.title}</h2>
              </div>
              <div class="mt-8 space-y-5 text-[17px] leading-[1.8] text-ivoire-muted md:pl-[3.25rem]">
                {s.blocks.map((block) => {
                  if (block.type === 'h3') {
                    return <h3 class="pt-3 font-serif text-2xl font-normal text-nuit">{block.text}</h3>;
                  }
                  if (block.type === 'ul') {
                    return (
                      <ul class="list-disc space-y-2.5 pl-6 marker:text-or">
                        {block.items.map((item) => <li set:html={item} />)}
                      </ul>
                    );
                  }
                  return <p set:html={block.html} />;
                })}
              </div>
            </article>
          ))}
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
</Base>
